  "seed_domain": "cozychat-noise-vectors-v1",
  "notes": [
    "Generated by the noiseprotocol package from fixed seeds; regenerate, never hand-edit.",
    "Private keys are the raw 32 bytes X25519 takes (clamped by X25519 itself, as in RFC 7748); public keys are derived from them.",
    "Messages are in wire order. The first two are the handshake; the rest are transport messages, each with empty associated data and its sender's next nonce.",
    "Rekey is by message count only: each side calls Noise Rekey() on its sending cipher after every rekey_interval messages it sent and on its receiving cipher after every rekey_interval messages it received; the nonce is not reset. Production uses 2^20; the rekey vector lowers it so the file can freeze messages across two rekeys each way.",
    "pairing_code.code = HMAC-SHA256(handshake_hash, 'cozychat-pair-code' || utf8(phone_name)) as a big-endian integer mod 10^6, zero-padded to 6 digits."
  ],
